    "at_a_glance": {
      "type": "multicolumn-with-icons",
      "blocks": {
        "g_time": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "time",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "About 50 minutes",
            "text": "<p>About 40 minutes &mdash; 15 of prep and 25 of cooking. The cucumber pickles and the sauce comes together while the r&ouml;sti and the salmon are in the heat, so very little of it is hands-on.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_serves": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "users",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Serves 4",
            "text": "<p>Serves one, from a single 6 oz Atlantic Salmon portion. It ships as a 2-Pack, so doubling everything gives you two bowls and uses the whole pack.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_prep": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "check_mark",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Watch for the C",
            "text": "<p>Wring the grated potato out in a towel until nothing more comes. Water is the enemy of a crisp r&ouml;sti &mdash; a damp pile steams into a soft pancake instead of separating into strands.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        },
        "g_marinade": {
          "type": "column",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "heart",
            "custom_icon": "",
            "heading": "Blended, not reduced",
            "text": "<p>The sauce is a deliberate double batch. Half coats the salmon and caramelises on it; half is spooned over cold at the end. Divide it <em>before</em> any of it touches raw fish.</p>",
            "highlighted_text": "none",
            "highlighted_scribble": "circle"
          }
        }
      },
